# Hifzhelper — cache policy (V3.6.2)
#
# This project is under active development, deployed manually and
# file-by-file (no atomic build step) — the state of the live site can
# change minute to minute, mid-deploy. V3.6 originally cached css/js/
# shared aggressively (immutable, one year), the standard pattern build
# tools like Webpack/Vite use — but that pattern is only safe when
# deploys are atomic, which this project's aren't. A browser that hit a
# versioned URL mid-deploy got stuck with the wrong content for a full
# year, with no way to fix it short of yet another version bump. See
# CONVENTIONS.md #10 for the full account.
#
# So: nothing is cached, anywhere, at all, for now. Every request always
# re-fetches from the origin. The ?v= query-string versioning in
# index.html/sw.js stays regardless — it's what breaks a cache that forms
# somewhere outside this project's control (a stray proxy, a CDN that
# ignores this header), and it's what long-lived caching would key off if
# it's ever worth reintroducing — once deploys are atomic, or this ships
# to real users where cache-hit-rate actually matters for performance.
# Neither is true yet.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
